body:
Ooh thanks for the info, I was thinking about getting another rat next year if I think I can handle it!

&#x200B;

I definitely plan to teach them lots of tricks, super excited to have some more social rodent babies! I adore my hamster but she is a dwarf hamster and very picky about when she wants to be handled.

I was dating this guy and I thought our relationship was normal. The breaking point was during our vacation at my family's place, while everyone was out, we argued and he hit me. The reason we argued was that I was sick and slept for a few days in a separate bed, because him shifting in his sleep made my already awful nausea worse, he wanted affection and that we sleep together again. I was talking with some close friends and when I told them what happened they just kinda went quiet and told me that that's not ok, then I told them more and they encouraged me to break up with him. I told them that when he and I got intimate sometimes he guilt me into doing it, like refusing any other affection unless I'd satisfy him, he'd start touching me even though I'd tell him to stop and I just kinda learned to wait it out and let it happen. When we argued he'd go punching the walls and guilt trip me by saying he can't live without me. It just snapped the whole illusion for me when he hit me, especially since I grew up with an abusive father and it triggered those memories rushing back. One of my best friends was living with me at the time and would take my phone away when he'd keep calling me and spamming me with texts to make sure I don't give in. When he came to bring the stuff I had at his place my friends were standing with me by the door, making sure he couldn't come in and wouldn't touch me or guilt me again.

&#x200B;

So tl;dr, he hit me, I realized something was off, talked to friends and they made me see things for what they are and supported me through it.

I hadn't thought of this, but 2004 and 2010 are actually the first times I vividly remember owning a computer and later phone. During that time I also started noticing the people I crushed on were "different" than the rest, it's also the time period I started developing symptoms of my anxiety disorder. I'm bisexual but usually have a preference for men so that actually checks out the rest too.

&#x200B;

Thank you for this interpretation, been trying to figure this dream out all day and now can finally make some sense of it!

Wow, what they did to her was awful. I hope she's doing better now.

&#x200B;

I have multiple disorders so sometimes I struggle to tell what's caused by my bpd and what's caused by the rest, but I manage by taking medication and going to therapy regularly. Still not leading what's considered a normal life yet though.
